title the ratchet reaches its floor
prompt Second of the two index folds Keaton named -- waymarks, 41 rows, its own round.
think Read the pin first again. All 41 rows link into date/, so the depth rewrite had one shape rather than two, and the fold was simpler than the prompts room.
think Both days had already folded into the room, so every row was stale and the living table would empty. Checked whether that is honest here rather than assuming: the one dated file still flat at the root is a bundle manifest, not a claim brief, so an empty claims table is the true reading.
think With waymarks enforced, every room this tree folds sits on the ENFORCE list, which puts the ratchet at zero. Kept the ratchet rather than deleting it -- it is the roof a room opened tomorrow arrives under, before a hand has read its front door.
obs 45 shelf links across two shelves, all resolving. Front door rewritten by hand: a shelf table holding the way in, then the living claims table with one plain line saying why it is empty.
obs The control's planted counts moved 41/42 -> 0/1 and the witness assertions with them. Planting one row against a ceiling of zero is a sharper bite than planting 42 against 41, so the floor reads better than the ceiling did.
obs The card crossed its declared bound by 155 bytes as the Now block grew, and declared_ceiling refused it rather than a hand noticing. Trimmed twice to 24,554. The guard doing the noticing is the whole point of REDS %197.
